<SPT><TTL>Augered Cast in Place Piles Installation</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>Payment</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Payment will be made for costs associated with installation of the required lengths of permanent augered cast 
in place piles, [including reinforcing steel,] [performing static load test, interpreting data and submitting 
reports,], compiling and submitting pile installation records, backfilling voids around piles, and any other 
items incidental to installing piles to the required elevation.  No payment will be made for installing piles 
exceeding required lengths.  No payment will be made for piles damaged during installation to the extent that 
they are rendered unsuitable for the work, in the opinion of the Contracting Officer.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>Measurement</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Permanent augered cast in place piles will be measured for payment for installation on the basis of lengths, 
to the nearest <MET>hundredth </MET><ENG>tenth </ENG>of a linear<MET> meter</MET><ENG> foot</ENG>, along the axis of each pile acceptably in place below 
the cut-off elevation shown as[determined by the Contracting Officer].</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>Unit of Measure</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Linear<MET> meter</MET><ENG> foot</ENG>.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
